{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_a9020f53eb9610f020f168c2d819b8c49efb6c531eb8455d8f19efc0952ce01d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the dev requirements file includes pytest and coverage>=7.2.5, indicating a Python test setup for contributors."}],"claim_ids":["clm_a9020f53eb9610f020f168c2d819b8c49efb6c531eb8455d8f19efc0952ce01d"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_980e2ba97ea94ebc96e13ab964b20e96","id":"pg_2eaab03352e05a14a79b1c458d7a56e7","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/lnxpy-hey-requirements-dev-txt-9b1b2ab680a4-1c458d7a56e7.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_783e940adfd653b796a00a0653af75fe"],"title":"lnxpy/hey/requirements-dev.txt @ 9b1b2ab680a4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_980e2ba97ea94ebc96e13ab964b20e96"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0105fcfcb789980bfd314e0a1e4a176dd9003de8ebea043a7fd7f76f0d53f9ca"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration is managed via `hey config create` to generate a base config file and `hey config edit` to view and edit it."},{"claim_ids":["clm_16fa087c47745e91a803a9d6535e1fbaa7e70826303e4b12a999419ee1e28586"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A `hey auth` command sets the LLM service token after installation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2348926268771b6b5835090c70c036e89764e800a95d7690d65ec6f7083676c3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README recommends free tokens from mdb.ai but notes users are not limited to it and can point Hey at any other LLM service."},{"claim_ids":["clm_333378e7c8a28c44c6a94f39c4bc55565bac508cf29fc7a1b0dbfcf190ef531d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration parameters include service URL, model (default gpt-3.5-turbo), a system prompt, code-block theme, loading text and spinner, and a never_style option to disable output styling for copying."},{"claim_ids":["clm_72ba22218f6adefa5aa6e43927134351a579d4e6971a5150baaa9d92b36e2b40"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The loading spinner feature appears to rely on the Rich library, since the config comment points users to `python -m rich.spinner` for the full spinner list."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7b5ccd553c40fc7bba18d94f85e3c4e845f37cb9482763baf41a1e42e800c593"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI provides an `ask` sub-command for quick questions, e.g. `hey ask \"...\"`, and `--help` to list commands and sub-commands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7df8aa6129c53f1d4841613d15f3cf72d417f0c6262aeddfe4f18ca0b4db50d2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Hey is a CLI-based AI assistant powered by LLMs, and users can choose which LLM service it connects to."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9f19a86280dc393eb4e4e237733611ab2d8b5a400bd855785a325acf8255da43"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The package is installable from PyPI as hey-mindsdb, or directly from the GitHub repository via pip."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bb0d8b5375f0971e262fb58b4faf497d70d400793eb8d39f91e00b04244693bb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool requires pip and Python 3.8 or newer on the user's machine."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e8b6b692ae46bef69eb47814217476045a01a632b8ed057a4a791f9db254830b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Running bare `hey` opens the default $EDITOR for composing longer questions; if unset, it falls back to vim on Unix-like systems and notepad on Windows."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0105fcfcb789980bfd314e0a1e4a176dd9003de8ebea043a7fd7f76f0d53f9ca","clm_16fa087c47745e91a803a9d6535e1fbaa7e70826303e4b12a999419ee1e28586","clm_2348926268771b6b5835090c70c036e89764e800a95d7690d65ec6f7083676c3","clm_333378e7c8a28c44c6a94f39c4bc55565bac508cf29fc7a1b0dbfcf190ef531d","clm_72ba22218f6adefa5aa6e43927134351a579d4e6971a5150baaa9d92b36e2b40","clm_7b5ccd553c40fc7bba18d94f85e3c4e845f37cb9482763baf41a1e42e800c593","clm_7df8aa6129c53f1d4841613d15f3cf72d417f0c6262aeddfe4f18ca0b4db50d2","clm_9f19a86280dc393eb4e4e237733611ab2d8b5a400bd855785a325acf8255da43","clm_bb0d8b5375f0971e262fb58b4faf497d70d400793eb8d39f91e00b04244693bb","clm_e8b6b692ae46bef69eb47814217476045a01a632b8ed057a4a791f9db254830b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_980e2ba97ea94ebc96e13ab964b20e96","id":"pg_4de467d49c015ee89baadc2e21850a70","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/lnxpy-hey-readme-md-9b1b2ab680a4-dc2e21850a70.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_b7c4790bbc7f56018b74c94f6233188b"],"title":"lnxpy/hey/README.md @ 9b1b2ab680a4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:06:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_980e2ba97ea94ebc96e13ab964b20e96"}
